.TH DIR_PATH 3
.SH NAME
dir_path \- construct the full path of a directory entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <dir.h>
.PP
.BI "void dir_path(struct dir_s* " d ", stralloc* " sa ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dir_path
constructs the full filesystem path for the current entry in the directory
structure
.I d
and appends it to the
.B stralloc
pointed to by
.IR sa .
.PP
The function retrieves the base directory path stored within the directory
context and appends the name of the currently accessed entry. If the base path
ends with a wildcard character, it is stripped before concatenation.
.PP
If wide character support is enabled (see
.B USE_WIDECHAR
in the project configuration), the function performs wide character to UTF-8
conversion to populate the
.B stralloc
correctly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dir_open (3),
.BR dir_next (3),
.BR stralloc (3)